# Cache-Control for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets — the replacement for the
# rules the old deploy wrote into Hostinger's .htaccess. Apache config does not
# travel with the site.
#
# Only ONE rule here, deliberately.
#
# Cloudflare already serves everything as `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# by default (verified against wrangler dev with this file emptied), which is
# exactly what HTML, images and PDFs need — none of them are content-hashed, so
# a stale copy is a real bug. That default is what protects us from repeating
# the Hostinger incident where HTML went out with no Cache-Control at all and a
# deploy stayed invisible for over a day. See CLAUDE.md.
#
# So a catch-all `/*` rule would be redundant — and worse than redundant:
# Cloudflare COMBINES every matching rule rather than letting the most specific
# one win, so `/*` plus `/_astro/*` produced
#     public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# on hashed assets. Browsers honour the first max-age, so the assets would
# never have been cached at all. Do not add a `/*` rule back.

# Astro's build output is content-hashed — the filename changes whenever the
# bytes do — so it is safe to cache forever. This is the one case where the
# default is wrong.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
